# This repository holds metadata only. Media is published separately —
# rsync to the server, or object storage — because it is written once and
# never edited, while git keeps every version of everything forever.
#
# One MV is larger than a decade of metadata here, so these patterns are a
# backstop against a stray `git add .`, not a preference.

*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.m4a
*.opus
*.ogg

*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv

*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.avif
*.gif

.DS_Store
